Sure: The relevant fragments of the guidebook (you got the guidebook with
your nethack distribution - didn't you?) read (reproduced without permisson):

          a    Apply (use) a tool (pick-axe, key, lamp...).

          M-i  Invoke an object's special powers.

Here we have it. (a)pply just makes you use the tool in a 'normal' way
(normal for that tool). Any tool can be (a)pplied. #invoke works only for
a few objects with special powers (not necessairly tools). The Orb of Fate
is a tool, and can be (a)pplied, like any normal orb. But it also has
some hidden powers - to get them you #invoke it. See the difference?

